  "name": "Question 6",
  "problem": "| ** Production  $\\,$ ($x$)** | **$24$** | **$27$** | **$30$** | **$31$** |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ** Price per $kg$  ($y$) ** | $2$ | $1.6$ | $1.4$ | $1.4$ |\n\nThe table above shows wheat production, in tons, and the average price of a kilogram of flour, in dollars, for a given country over the last four years. The corresponding linear regression line fitted using this sample is $\\overset{^}{\\,y}=4-0.1x.$\nAssuming that all conditions for the simple regression model are satisfied, $\\overset{―}{x}=28,$ and $\\text{MSE}=0.007,$ find a $90%$ confidence interval for the slope of the regression line.   \n\n*Hint: Use the fact that $P(T>2.92)=0.05,$ where $T$ has a student's $t$-distribution with $2$ degrees of freedom. Also, the standard error for the slope is given by* \n\n$$\n\\text{SE}[{\\overset{^}{\\,\\beta }}_{1}\\,]=\\sqrt{\\frac{\\text{MSE}}{{S}_{xx}}}.\n$$",
